         <t:abstract><t:p>Hymn composed on the occasion of the consecration of the church of Dabra Bǝrhān Śǝllāse (1694 A.D.) and attributed to <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8671SebhatL">ʾAbbā Sǝbḥat Laʾab</t:persName> (†1702 A.D.).</t:p>
            <t:p>According to <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/X4SBAXAT"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Loefgren1974Katalog"/><title level="m">Katalog über die äthiopischen Handschriften in der Universitätsbibliothek Uppsala, Sowie Anhänge über äthiopische Handschriften in anderen Bibliotheken und in Privatbesitz in Schweden</title><title level="s">Acta Bibliothecae R. Universitatis Upsaliensis</title><author><forename>Oscar</forename><surname>Löfgren</surname></author><pubPlace>Uppsala</pubPlace><publisher>Almqvist &amp; Wiksell</publisher><date>1974</date><series><title level="s">Acta Bibliothecae R. Universitatis Upsaliensis</title><biblScope unit="volume">18</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">18</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Loefgren1974Katalog</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Loefgren1974Katalog</note><t:citedRange unit="page">45</t:citedRange></t:bibl>,
               the text was written under one <t:foreign xml:lang="gez-tr">nǝguś</t:foreign> ʾIyāsu mentioned in the 
               <t:foreign xml:lang="gez-tr">malkǝʾ</t:foreign>, i.e. either under 
               <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5616IyasuI">ʾIyāsu I (r. 1682–1706)</t:persName> or
               <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5617IyasuII">ʾIyāsu II (r. 1730–1755)</t:persName>.</t:p>
         </t:abstract>
